# Fraud-Detection

This project contains a FastAPI backend for fraud prediction and a static frontend dashboard.

## Local development

1. Install dependencies:
   ```bash
   pip install -r requirements.txt
   ```

2. Start the backend:
   ```bash
   python -m uvicorn backend.main:app --reload --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000
   ```

3. Open the frontend in a browser from the `frontend` directory or serve the app through the FastAPI app at the root URL.

## Deployment

The app is designed to run on deployment platforms such as Render, Railway, or similar services using the included `Procfile`:

```Procfile
web: uvicorn backend.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port $PORT
```

### Required environment variables

Set the following variables in your deployment platform:

```bash
CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://your-frontend-domain.com,https://www.your-frontend-domain.com
```

If the frontend is hosted from the same origin as the API, you can leave `CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` unset and the app will default to allowing all origins during development.

For a separate frontend deployment, configure the frontend to point to the backend URL:

```html
<meta name="api-url" content="https://your-backend-domain.com">
```

or before the app script runs:

```html
<script>
  window.__API_URL__ = "https://your-backend-domain.com";
</script>
```

## API endpoints

- `GET /` — app status
- `GET /health` — health check
- `POST /predict` — fraud prediction

